WEBVTT

00:42.042 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

00:52.510 --> 00:53.511
Let's go.

00:56.848 --> 00:58.850
MEMORIAL GATE

01:01.853 --> 01:03.938
Chief, I'm sorry. Excuse me for a moment.

01:08.693 --> 01:09.903
Yes, what is it?

01:09.986 --> 01:12.030
This is Yongju Silver Care Hospital.

01:12.113 --> 01:14.574
We can't locate Mr. Na Jin-cheol.

01:14.657 --> 01:18.161
Your number was listed
as the emergency contact, so I called you.

01:18.244 --> 01:20.246
Okay, I'll be right there.

01:22.665 --> 01:24.125
What's the matter?

01:25.668 --> 01:28.379
There seems to be an issue
with my father-in-law.

01:28.463 --> 01:29.923
Oh, no. Then you should hurry.

01:30.006 --> 01:34.302
Use my official vehicle.
They'll get you there quickly and safely.

01:54.447 --> 01:55.615
Oh, dear.

01:55.698 --> 01:56.908
Are you okay?

02:04.833 --> 02:05.750
What?

02:07.252 --> 02:09.838
Why are they coming towards us?

02:10.421 --> 02:12.423
- Did we do something wrong?
- No way!

02:12.507 --> 02:13.591
We didn't do anything.

02:36.531 --> 02:38.908
Hello. Thank you for your hard work.

02:39.617 --> 02:41.578
You may leave now.

02:41.661 --> 02:42.620
Pardon?

02:42.704 --> 02:45.165
I'll come to the station
to file the report.

02:45.248 --> 02:48.960
I'm sorry,
but what's your relationship with her?

02:49.669 --> 02:50.753
We're family.

02:51.379 --> 02:52.338
Excuse me?

02:59.596 --> 03:00.805
She is…

03:02.307 --> 03:03.266
my wife.

03:09.814 --> 03:10.815
Stay here.

03:13.192 --> 03:15.653
- My wife gave this case to me.
- He's Paik Sa-eon.

03:18.907 --> 03:20.533
I have a favor to ask.

03:21.367 --> 03:23.161
Yes, please go ahead.

03:23.244 --> 03:25.955
I'll visit as soon as I can
to file the report.

03:26.039 --> 03:30.376
In the meantime, please keep
our personal information private.

03:30.460 --> 03:32.337
Yes, of course.

03:32.420 --> 03:35.006
We'll ensure strict security.

03:35.965 --> 03:36.966
Thank you.

03:37.050 --> 03:38.051
By the way…

03:38.134 --> 03:41.512
- Don't do it. Don't.
- I also have a favor to ask.

03:41.596 --> 03:44.724
I know this isn't the greatest situation,

03:45.225 --> 03:47.352
but may I get a picture with you?

03:49.062 --> 03:50.605
If you keep your promise,

03:50.688 --> 03:53.191
I'll take a picture with you
at the station.

03:53.775 --> 03:55.026
I see. Okay.

03:55.610 --> 03:57.904
- Well, then.
- Okay, see you again.

03:58.613 --> 03:59.614
Go safely.

04:17.924 --> 04:19.634
Your father's nurse…

04:20.718 --> 04:22.136
has my number.

04:23.304 --> 04:26.724
Anyway, we should move him
to a different nursing home.

04:31.646 --> 04:33.022
How could he go so far?

04:36.401 --> 04:37.402
From now on,

04:39.153 --> 04:41.281
you don't have to worry about your father.

04:42.073 --> 04:43.324
I'll take care of it.

05:01.592 --> 05:03.469
You're making sounds.

05:10.435 --> 05:11.394
Hong Hee-joo…

05:12.937 --> 05:14.272
can make sounds.

05:26.784 --> 05:28.161
You look so ugly right now.

05:36.044 --> 05:37.837
I'm not telling you to stop crying.

05:40.548 --> 05:41.924
Cry as much as you want.

06:10.953 --> 06:14.290
One tteokbokki set with gimbap,
fish cakes, and sundae with the entrails.

06:14.373 --> 06:15.625
Can I have one?

06:16.250 --> 06:17.210
Come more often!

06:17.293 --> 06:18.586
- Okay?
- I'm here!

06:18.669 --> 06:21.005
I'm just happy to see you.

06:22.507 --> 06:24.175
You get prettier by the day.

06:24.258 --> 06:25.468
I was always pretty.

06:26.677 --> 06:29.555
- Are you just getting off work?
- My goodness.

06:31.224 --> 06:33.726
We don't have a show today.
What brings you here?

06:34.310 --> 06:35.561
Well…

06:35.645 --> 06:37.105
Oh, my.

06:37.772 --> 06:38.898
Don't tell me…

06:39.982 --> 06:41.818
Did you come hoping to run into me?

06:42.985 --> 06:43.945
Come on.

06:44.028 --> 06:46.697
We're visiting a site together
in a few days!

06:55.206 --> 06:56.207
I was kidding.

06:58.793 --> 07:00.044
Do you live in Yeouido?

07:00.878 --> 07:02.547
Yeah, it's near the hospital.

07:04.465 --> 07:05.633
Thank you.

07:08.970 --> 07:09.804
Is it…

07:11.264 --> 07:12.306
your birthday today?

07:12.390 --> 07:14.600
- What?
- That looks like a feast.

07:15.435 --> 07:18.104
This is one serving for me.

07:18.187 --> 07:19.439
I see.

07:20.606 --> 07:24.986
That day at the French restaurant,
it didn't even make a dent in my stomach.

07:25.862 --> 07:26.737
Eat up.

07:36.539 --> 07:37.373
Hey.

07:39.667 --> 07:41.085
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo.

07:42.128 --> 07:43.087
It's her, isn't it?

07:43.838 --> 07:45.047
Your secret crush.

07:52.138 --> 07:53.848
I could just tell that day.

07:53.931 --> 07:57.351
You said you've been through
unrequited love like a fan before.

07:57.435 --> 07:58.352
Remember?

07:59.770 --> 08:02.440
Well… I'm curious about something too.

08:02.523 --> 08:03.733
Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon.

08:04.400 --> 08:06.569
Why are you such a big fan of him?

08:08.404 --> 08:09.489
Well…

08:10.531 --> 08:11.365
Me?

08:13.576 --> 08:15.411
I didn't like him at first.

08:16.662 --> 08:19.373
Actually, I was so scared of him.

08:19.457 --> 08:20.458
ON AIR

08:20.541 --> 08:24.504
Are you saying there are no standards
to regulate microplastics?

08:24.587 --> 08:29.050
Yes, a bill must be prepared
through National Assembly discussions.

08:29.759 --> 08:31.969
That's all that I've prepared.

08:32.053 --> 08:36.390
Then, what could be
realistic regulatory measures?

08:37.475 --> 08:38.392
Excuse me?

08:39.810 --> 08:41.145
MICROPLASTIC SWALLOWING THE OCEAN

08:41.229 --> 08:42.063
Well…

08:43.231 --> 08:47.818
First, we should reduce plastic use
and use tumblers instead of disposables.

08:47.902 --> 08:51.531
That would be more of an individual effort
and a recommendation.

08:52.240 --> 08:55.076
What could be legally prohibited?

08:55.159 --> 08:56.452
Well…

08:57.745 --> 08:59.372
Well…

09:01.332 --> 09:02.416
Anchor Na You-ri?

09:03.042 --> 09:04.919
Aside from just raising the issue,

09:05.002 --> 09:07.880
are there no concrete solutions prepared?

09:10.424 --> 09:14.011
Well… I…

09:15.304 --> 09:17.181
He's breaking in a new recruit again.

09:17.682 --> 09:19.475
She looks like she'll cry.

09:22.687 --> 09:24.480
Thank you for your presentation.

09:40.830 --> 09:42.415
Come in by two o'clock from tomorrow.

09:44.125 --> 09:46.002
You mean, two o'clock in the morning?

09:47.837 --> 09:52.133
If you're to run it by me for review,
learn how to write it, and practice,

09:52.717 --> 09:53.843
it's not that early.

09:54.427 --> 09:57.972
You'll teach me yourself?

10:00.141 --> 10:03.561
An anchor isn't a parrot
that simply reads off a script.

10:04.228 --> 10:08.733
Plus, for the morning news, you should
come in by two to remove facial swelling.

10:10.359 --> 10:13.487
Look at your face now.
You look like a soggy steamed bun.

10:22.204 --> 10:23.831
He was scary,

10:24.707 --> 10:27.418
but he was a good colleague
who taught me a lot.

10:30.796 --> 10:31.964
But then one day,

10:32.048 --> 10:34.800
he quit his job
and got appointed as spokesperson.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.093
He even got married.

10:36.177 --> 10:39.513
- Now it's hard to see him once a year.
- Who did he marry?

10:54.320 --> 10:57.948
Sa-eon's family
is a famous political family.

10:58.032 --> 11:01.577
His grandfather's a bigwig who's done
everything except for the presidency.

11:01.661 --> 11:03.454
His father's
a strong presidential candidate.

11:03.537 --> 11:05.748
His relatives are
former or current ministers,

11:05.831 --> 11:07.500
prosecutor generals, mayors, lawmakers…

11:07.583 --> 11:10.586
Naturally, he married the daughter
of a very influential family.

11:11.837 --> 11:15.424
The eldest daughter of Chairman Hong
of Chungwoon Daily News.

11:29.772 --> 11:32.733
Did you just remember
what day it is today?

11:40.074 --> 11:41.283
Why a hotel room?

11:41.367 --> 11:43.452
Wash your face. And blow your nose too.

11:53.212 --> 11:54.839
Yes, this is room service.

12:15.151 --> 12:16.694
I need to get it together.

12:17.278 --> 12:19.864
I have to stay focused from now on.

12:30.958 --> 12:32.293
Should we talk now?

12:33.252 --> 12:34.086
Sit down.

12:37.882 --> 12:38.966
Take out your phone.

12:40.176 --> 12:41.343
Because from now on,

12:42.344 --> 12:43.804
I want us to have a conversation.

12:45.848 --> 12:48.100
- Not an interrogation?
- It's not an interrogation.

12:50.186 --> 12:51.270
As you know,

12:52.605 --> 12:55.024
someone's been messing with us lately.

12:56.025 --> 12:58.110
Your car, my office,

12:58.194 --> 13:00.613
and even your father's nursing home
this time.

13:01.155 --> 13:03.324
I haven't requested
a police investigation yet.

13:04.325 --> 13:05.534
But if this continues,

13:06.368 --> 13:07.703
I'll have no other choice.

13:12.291 --> 13:16.545
If you're the victim instead of me,
the police will start digging into you.

13:16.629 --> 13:21.133
So before that happens,
tell me if you're hiding anything.

13:27.890 --> 13:29.391
I guess there is something.

13:35.481 --> 13:39.610
I could keep pressuring you
until I force it out of you, but…

13:41.487 --> 13:42.321
I won't.

13:43.739 --> 13:45.324
I won't do that, Hee-joo.

13:46.700 --> 13:48.452
We're not close enough to interfere

13:49.578 --> 13:51.372
with each other's lives, right?

13:57.294 --> 13:58.379
Leave it at the door.

14:15.229 --> 14:18.816
Eat this and rest.
Come down afterward. I'll go first.

14:29.743 --> 14:31.412
You haven't settled from the shock yet.

14:31.996 --> 14:35.541
You know you'll be very tense down there.

14:38.252 --> 14:40.754
Don't overdo it. Just do as I say.

15:26.800 --> 15:27.635
Another glass.

15:40.856 --> 15:41.982
Relax.

15:43.609 --> 15:44.443
What?

15:49.406 --> 15:50.616
Ouch.

15:52.868 --> 15:54.370
Do you have a plan?

16:00.125 --> 16:03.170
It shouldn't just be
another regular meal today, right?

16:04.421 --> 16:06.215
Didn't the aides make a plan?

16:06.298 --> 16:08.300
I don't need a grand plan for this.

16:09.301 --> 16:11.053
A disobedient child?

16:11.136 --> 16:12.888
Just beat him until he obeys.

16:14.723 --> 16:15.724
Don't worry.

16:40.249 --> 16:41.375
You're here.

16:44.753 --> 16:45.713
Why are you alone?

16:46.505 --> 16:47.339
Where is she?

16:49.717 --> 16:50.926
She's not feeling well.

16:51.010 --> 16:51.927
Call her.

16:56.265 --> 16:57.182
Did you not hear me?

16:57.891 --> 16:59.518
Bring her here right now.

16:59.601 --> 17:00.978
Let's eat.

17:01.854 --> 17:03.856
I only have an hour to spare.

17:05.024 --> 17:07.651
Didn't you have something to say to me?

17:40.059 --> 17:41.810
Appear on a show?

17:41.894 --> 17:42.728
Yeah.

17:43.562 --> 17:46.857
A special on presidential candidates.
Just anyone does it these days.

17:47.441 --> 17:50.611
You know, cooking, dancing, and singing.

17:54.114 --> 17:55.324
Come when we're filming.

18:04.500 --> 18:05.876
Come and sit.

18:15.803 --> 18:18.597
Others bring their sons, daughters-in-law,

18:18.680 --> 18:22.434
and even their dogs and cats
to promote themselves.

18:23.685 --> 18:24.728
But our family…

18:25.479 --> 18:28.148
The only thing I can boast about
is my son.

18:29.775 --> 18:32.611
Have you still not heard from your sister?

18:32.694 --> 18:34.154
Don't bring that up again.

18:34.238 --> 18:37.324
You know, I really think
Chairman Hong tricked me.

18:37.407 --> 18:40.828
He never intended to give us
his eldest daughter in the first place.

18:40.911 --> 18:43.163
Right? He's so skeptical.

18:43.914 --> 18:45.833
He's scared I might lose the election.

18:45.916 --> 18:48.752
That's why he sent
his flawed daughter as a stand-in.

18:50.963 --> 18:52.506
What exactly is your purpose?

18:53.257 --> 18:56.385
Even if you were a bargain,
you should be able to earn your keep.

18:57.010 --> 18:58.971
Why can't you do anything?

19:04.309 --> 19:05.435
What are you doing?

19:06.103 --> 19:07.646
It's rude. We're eating.

19:08.647 --> 19:09.606
Bring it.

19:23.662 --> 19:24.955
Welcome.

19:26.790 --> 19:29.418
There's a paparazzi
taking pictures of guests here.

19:33.755 --> 19:37.009
"Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon meets with
his father, Paik Ui-yong, for dinner."

19:37.968 --> 19:39.887
"Will he join the election campaign?"

19:40.929 --> 19:42.431
Is that the headline you wanted?

19:44.683 --> 19:47.603
I'll decide whether or not to participate
in your election.

19:47.686 --> 19:50.105
Coercion, threats, subtle manipulation.

19:50.189 --> 19:51.523
Don't even think of it.

19:54.151 --> 19:55.652
You little punk.

20:11.919 --> 20:13.295
You arrogant brat.

20:16.048 --> 20:17.466
You punk.

20:17.549 --> 20:20.385
Do you know what will happen
if you keep acting like this?

20:21.053 --> 20:24.932
The moment you step out of my shadow,
you could get crushed completely.

20:26.099 --> 20:28.977
Do you really think I'm still in there?

20:29.061 --> 20:30.145
What did you say?

20:33.190 --> 20:34.024
Wait.

20:35.609 --> 20:36.693
It's not you, is it?

20:36.777 --> 20:37.694
What do you mean?

20:38.528 --> 20:41.073
I know you'd do anything
to get me to surrender.

20:42.157 --> 20:44.826
- So the thought crossed my mind.
- What are you talking about?

20:44.910 --> 20:46.161
Make some damn sense!

20:50.415 --> 20:51.875
I'll say one thing.

20:53.001 --> 20:55.671
You're at the threshold
of being president, thanks to Grandfather.

20:55.754 --> 20:59.132
The least you could do
is step over it on your own.

20:59.216 --> 21:00.759
Don't whine

21:01.718 --> 21:03.011
and ask me to push you.

21:04.388 --> 21:05.222
What?

21:08.976 --> 21:10.852
- Are you done?
- I am.

21:13.563 --> 21:14.898
And I'll leave now.

21:22.322 --> 21:23.907
Was this your plan?

21:24.992 --> 21:26.243
You ruined everything.

21:28.161 --> 21:30.122
That punk started it!

21:32.165 --> 21:33.208
Damn it.

21:34.209 --> 21:35.460
That damned punk.

21:48.557 --> 21:49.558
I bet you…

21:50.475 --> 21:51.893
want to divorce me.

21:54.062 --> 21:56.815
You married me in place
of your missing sister and can't speak.

21:57.399 --> 22:00.110
So you can't even defend yourself
when your in-laws spout nonsense.

22:06.408 --> 22:08.994
They're people
who can easily replace their children.

22:09.661 --> 22:10.912
So whatever they say,

22:11.872 --> 22:14.875
don't listen to them or take it to heart.

22:23.258 --> 22:26.386
PARK DO-JAE

22:28.472 --> 22:29.306
Go inside.

22:38.065 --> 22:39.191
Yes, go ahead.

22:40.901 --> 22:43.945
The detective in charge
of the nursing home incident just called.

22:44.029 --> 22:47.324
He said the blood analysis results
confirmed animal blood and fake teeth.

22:47.407 --> 22:48.575
Animal?

22:53.371 --> 22:54.831
Okay.

22:54.915 --> 22:58.585
Also, I have a personal request.

23:08.178 --> 23:10.263
Call…

23:10.347 --> 23:12.724
Call him.

23:14.101 --> 23:16.770
Sis.

23:19.022 --> 23:21.733
No backing out in the middle.

23:22.609 --> 23:24.402
You started this,

23:25.529 --> 23:26.905
so you see it through.

23:26.988 --> 23:28.281
Got it?

23:28.365 --> 23:31.827
Sis!

23:34.955 --> 23:35.789
I can't…

23:36.790 --> 23:38.333
do this anymore.

23:56.184 --> 23:57.227
Where are you going?

24:00.522 --> 24:01.356
Is that trash?

24:02.607 --> 24:03.441
Give it to me.

24:06.444 --> 24:07.529
I'll take it out.

24:24.254 --> 24:26.423
DIRECTOR HAN JIN-E

24:28.008 --> 24:29.551
- Hey, Hee-joo!
- Hee-joo!

24:30.635 --> 24:32.888
You can do this! Good luck! You got this!

24:32.971 --> 24:33.889
Good luck!

24:33.972 --> 24:34.848
Let's go!

24:34.931 --> 24:36.850
To the president's office!

24:38.268 --> 24:39.769
Thanks, everyone.

24:39.853 --> 24:41.104
Don't mention it.

24:41.771 --> 24:43.106
Dinner's on you if you pass!

24:43.190 --> 24:44.774
Good luck! We love you!

24:47.152 --> 24:48.570
I'll wish you luck too.

24:48.653 --> 24:49.946
You'll pass.

24:58.330 --> 24:59.998
If I get it, what then?

25:02.209 --> 25:03.543
What do you mean?

25:05.378 --> 25:06.880
We talked about this before.

25:06.963 --> 25:09.883
If our families find out
I'm working beside you…

25:09.966 --> 25:11.134
Hong Hee-joo.

25:12.427 --> 25:15.055
How much longer
will you live as the obedient child?

25:15.889 --> 25:17.849
Aren't you sick of others
telling you what to do?

25:18.683 --> 25:20.894
It's your chance to try
with your name on the line.

25:21.811 --> 25:24.856
Chicken out and blow it
or give up over what others think.

25:25.899 --> 25:26.816
Do whatever you want.

25:36.910 --> 25:39.079
Okay, then you should start thinking about

25:39.162 --> 25:42.332
how you're going to handle
the aftermath if I get the job.

26:04.437 --> 26:05.855
PARK DO-JAE

26:07.607 --> 26:10.402
I looked into what you asked for.

26:12.153 --> 26:15.031
CLASSY COUNTY
WE MEET ANOTHER FAMILY MEMBER TODAY

26:21.121 --> 26:22.747
Looks good. Let's go with this.

26:39.055 --> 26:42.434
Our spokesperson has never been this late
to work before.

26:42.517 --> 26:43.977
Is something wrong?

26:44.060 --> 26:46.563
He has matters to take care of,
so he'll be late.

26:52.944 --> 26:54.779
- Hello.
- Hello.

27:03.204 --> 27:05.373
- I have something to report.
- Me too.

27:06.082 --> 27:07.625
It's urgent. I'll go first.

27:07.709 --> 27:08.710
Mine's urgent too.

27:09.919 --> 27:11.046
Mr. Park.

27:11.129 --> 27:12.047
Yes, sir.

27:25.185 --> 27:26.353
I'm the section chief.

27:28.271 --> 27:31.441
I have something to discuss
regarding the voice modulation.

27:31.524 --> 27:32.692
Did you find something?

27:32.776 --> 27:35.070
If we analyze
the waveform and spectrogram,

27:35.153 --> 27:38.907
I think we'll be able to determine
the pitch range, age, and gender.

27:38.990 --> 27:40.283
We don't need the gender.

27:40.867 --> 27:43.453
To be honest, I'm not curious
about that pervert's voice.

27:44.120 --> 27:46.581
Just in case, it might be someone I know.

27:46.664 --> 27:48.583
- That's why I want to unmask him.
- Okay.

27:48.666 --> 27:50.460
I'll report it as soon as it's done.

27:50.960 --> 27:51.795
Okay.

27:51.878 --> 27:54.297
And this is regarding Ji Sang-woo.

27:56.674 --> 27:57.926
A lot of his videos

27:58.009 --> 28:00.804
are about unsolved cases
related to arson and bombs.

28:00.887 --> 28:04.349
He seems to be very knowledgeable
about explosions and arson methods.

28:05.058 --> 28:07.727
And currently,
he's appearing on HBC's Crime Report.

28:07.811 --> 28:09.979
It's a mystery crime program.

28:11.231 --> 28:12.399
"Crime Report"?

28:16.528 --> 28:17.654
Okay.

28:17.737 --> 28:19.155
- You're excused.
- Yes, sir.

28:28.915 --> 28:29.999
Sir.

28:30.917 --> 28:33.670
It's the final interview list
for the sign language interpreters.

28:35.588 --> 28:36.589
HONG HEE-JOO

28:37.173 --> 28:39.634
The interviews will start soon.
Will you join?

28:47.475 --> 28:48.727
CANDIDATE ID
HONG HEE-JOO

28:49.853 --> 28:52.480
It's your chance to try
with your name on the line.

28:52.564 --> 28:55.442
Chicken out and blow it
or give up over what others think.

28:56.568 --> 28:57.652
Do whatever you want.

29:05.201 --> 29:08.788
Candidate 24, 25, and 26, please be ready.

29:14.919 --> 29:18.006
2024 PRESIDENTIAL OFFICE
SIGN LANGUAGE INTERPRETER INTERVIEW

29:19.007 --> 29:21.760
You'll conduct a real briefing
for the final interview.

29:21.843 --> 29:23.261
It'll be a practical exam.

29:23.344 --> 29:25.096
In case of real-time interpretation,

29:25.180 --> 29:28.725
quick thinking and sign language speed
are especially important.

29:28.808 --> 29:31.019
I'll play an existing briefing video.

29:31.102 --> 29:32.103
Candidate…

29:32.812 --> 29:35.648
number 24, Hong Hee-joo,
we'll start with you.

29:43.114 --> 29:44.199
PRESIDENTIAL OFFICE

29:49.245 --> 29:52.040
The 2020 Korea-Egypt summit briefing.

29:52.123 --> 29:55.710
Korea and Egypt
have complementary industrial structures,

29:55.794 --> 29:59.047
which offer great potential
for expanding trade and investment.

29:59.130 --> 29:59.964
It is hoped that

30:00.048 --> 30:03.134
the Korea-Egypt Trade and Economic
Partnership Joint Research MOU

30:03.218 --> 30:05.512
will lead to an FTA
between the two countries.

30:05.595 --> 30:08.807
Also, it was expressed that there's hope
for cooperative projects

30:08.890 --> 30:11.017
to strengthen administrative capabilities

30:11.100 --> 30:13.895
by sharing South Korea's
digital information expertise.

30:13.978 --> 30:16.815
Furthermore, both countries agreed
to open a new chapter

30:16.898 --> 30:20.568
of mutually beneficial cooperation
in key areas such as economic investment,

30:20.652 --> 30:23.112
cultural heritage preservation
and management,

30:23.196 --> 30:26.282
energy, advanced technologies,
and defense,

30:26.366 --> 30:29.118
aiming to establish
a comprehensive partnership

30:29.202 --> 30:31.037
between the two nations.

30:31.120 --> 30:34.624
As emphasized, this will boost
our country's overall competitiveness.

30:35.208 --> 30:36.209
Thank you.

30:40.129 --> 30:40.964
Excuse me.

30:43.424 --> 30:44.259
Yes?

30:46.427 --> 30:47.637
I understand.

30:51.850 --> 30:53.434
SPOKESPERSON BRIEFING

31:25.675 --> 31:28.428
Candidate number 24,
interpreter Hong Hee-joo.

31:28.511 --> 31:32.140
I want you to answer
the questions I ask honestly.

31:34.100 --> 31:36.269
Did you know the script in advance?

31:36.352 --> 31:38.479
It wasn't simultaneous interpretation.

31:38.563 --> 31:41.983
I noticed that you signed
before I even spoke sometimes.

31:42.734 --> 31:44.068
How will you explain this?

31:46.112 --> 31:47.864
I practiced to these videos.

31:49.991 --> 31:50.992
If that's the case,

31:52.118 --> 31:54.787
can we test you with a different video?

31:55.496 --> 31:56.331
Yes.

32:08.635 --> 32:10.303
For a healthy society,

32:10.386 --> 32:15.600
all citizens must unite
in caring for and educating children.

32:15.683 --> 32:19.812
This is something that all members
of society must participate in.

32:19.896 --> 32:20.772
Enough.

32:20.855 --> 32:22.023
Next video.

32:22.649 --> 32:25.652
Our government has consistently expressed
its willingness

32:25.735 --> 32:27.862
to engage in dialogue
to resolve the issue.

32:27.946 --> 32:29.364
- Next.
- Diplomatic communication…

32:30.031 --> 32:33.701
In the current situation where
business leaders are facing difficulties

32:33.785 --> 32:37.372
and everyone is trying their best
in their respective positions,

32:37.455 --> 32:39.499
- we must answer what truly…
- Next.

32:39.582 --> 32:40.708
…serves the people…

32:40.792 --> 32:43.920
To prevent further harm
to the victim's reputation

32:44.003 --> 32:47.882
through reports where even the facts
have not been verified,

32:47.966 --> 32:50.385
I ask that journalists exercise caution.

32:52.595 --> 32:54.138
Did you practice to all of these?

32:56.683 --> 32:57.517
Yes.

32:59.143 --> 33:02.647
It'll be the same
with any other video you play.

33:03.898 --> 33:06.067
Why have you memorized all the videos?

33:06.859 --> 33:10.989
I practiced a lot with your videos.

33:11.614 --> 33:14.909
They were chosen at random,
regardless of the year or content.

33:14.993 --> 33:18.371
But your hands move at the same speed
and timing as my voice.

33:18.997 --> 33:21.416
Is that a coincidence?
It's not just once or twice.

33:22.834 --> 33:25.294
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo,
answer my question.

33:37.890 --> 33:40.727
What did you just say?

33:42.812 --> 33:44.230
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo!

33:49.485 --> 33:52.363
I said I did it because I was crazy.

33:52.447 --> 33:53.531
Wow.

33:53.614 --> 33:54.532
She was crazy.

33:58.327 --> 34:01.706
I was obsessed
with your briefings, Mr. Paik.

34:02.290 --> 34:06.461
I've dreamed of becoming a sign language
interpreter for a government agency.

34:06.544 --> 34:08.129
That became excessive…

34:08.212 --> 34:10.465
This is the result of intense practicing?

34:10.548 --> 34:13.468
How your upper lip and upper teeth move

34:13.551 --> 34:17.597
when you set your articulation points,
I studied that a lot in particular.

34:17.680 --> 34:18.931
I can predict consonants

34:19.015 --> 34:22.101
from the sounds your tongue makes
against the roof of your mouth.

34:22.185 --> 34:24.479
So, as soon as I open my mouth…

34:24.562 --> 34:25.396
No, wait.

34:26.189 --> 34:29.025
Your hands move faster
when you predict it?

34:29.609 --> 34:32.195
And you studied it that obsessively?

34:32.278 --> 34:36.783
I mimicked, practiced, and dug into it.

34:42.371 --> 34:43.372
But…

34:43.956 --> 34:46.084
can you not speak at all?

34:50.296 --> 34:52.799
Personal disabilities
aren't disqualifying factors,

34:52.882 --> 34:54.634
so she passed the document review.

34:55.343 --> 34:59.889
And the job of an interpreter is to listen
and convey it with their hands, so…

35:00.389 --> 35:01.808
If you get the job,

35:01.891 --> 35:05.478
how will you communicate
with the spokesperson's team?

35:14.362 --> 35:19.367
2024 PRESIDENTIAL OFFICE
SIGN LANGUAGE INTERPRETER INTERVIEW

35:21.661 --> 35:23.579
I don't know why, but he's fixated.

35:24.163 --> 35:25.289
It might take a while.

35:27.083 --> 35:28.960
The interview is running behind.

35:29.043 --> 35:30.670
I hope you understand.

35:38.386 --> 35:41.222
Can you use sign language?

35:41.305 --> 35:43.766
If you can't, I'll teach you.

35:43.850 --> 35:45.768
You need to learn so you can see

35:45.852 --> 35:48.813
whether we interpreters are conveying
your message properly.

35:49.397 --> 35:52.358
If the nuance is off,
you can correct it right away.

35:52.441 --> 35:54.277
Sign language isn't difficult.

35:54.902 --> 35:58.698
If you learn it, there won't be issues
communicating with me either.

35:58.781 --> 36:01.284
You're right. That's a good idea.

36:05.496 --> 36:07.582
We'll discuss that if you get the job.

36:08.457 --> 36:09.375
Finally,

36:10.042 --> 36:11.669
I want to test you on something.

36:12.336 --> 36:14.797
I'll read a document
that you've never seen before,

36:14.881 --> 36:16.382
on the spot.

36:17.300 --> 36:18.801
Can you do it?

36:20.219 --> 36:21.053
Yes.

36:22.096 --> 36:23.931
Then, let's begin.

36:29.312 --> 36:30.146
Couple's Day…

36:31.772 --> 36:34.192
is a national observance
established to remind us

36:35.151 --> 36:38.070
of the importance of marital relationships
and to encourage

36:38.154 --> 36:39.906
the building of harmonious families.

36:41.199 --> 36:43.618
There's a couple here now.

36:46.621 --> 36:50.291
The two have lived
without being able to open up

36:51.167 --> 36:52.418
to each other.

36:56.547 --> 36:58.216
Would things have been different…

37:00.718 --> 37:02.803
if they had been more honest

37:04.222 --> 37:05.598
and shown their true feelings?

37:08.392 --> 37:10.102
If they try to make an effort now,

37:11.979 --> 37:14.607
could they live
like any other ordinary couple?

37:17.568 --> 37:18.903
Yet again today,

37:20.029 --> 37:21.280
like how a mind game is played,

37:22.365 --> 37:24.533
the couple merely tries to read
each other's minds.

37:25.326 --> 37:26.827
The ironic thing is that

37:28.412 --> 37:31.832
their behavior is surprisingly similar.

37:54.188 --> 37:55.022
That's enough.

37:55.898 --> 37:57.191
Let's stop here.

38:18.421 --> 38:21.716
I can assure you,
there's no one better than me.

38:22.466 --> 38:24.343
I can tell by a person's expression.

38:24.427 --> 38:27.388
I know what you're going to say
and what you're thinking.

38:29.557 --> 38:33.352
I mimicked, practiced, and dug into it.

38:36.105 --> 38:37.106
Hong Hee-joo.

38:39.817 --> 38:40.901
What are you…

38:56.625 --> 38:58.961
CANDIDATE ID
HONG HEE-JOO

39:04.091 --> 39:05.718
I did a good job.

39:06.927 --> 39:07.928
Well done.

39:47.093 --> 39:49.387
Classy County?

39:51.639 --> 39:53.641
We should move him
to a different nursing home.

39:56.602 --> 39:58.270
- …work this much?
- Tell me about it.

39:59.230 --> 40:00.731
He's an anchor.

40:01.524 --> 40:02.900
You weren't a farmer?

40:02.983 --> 40:06.195
That'll be hard in old age too.

40:06.278 --> 40:07.279
So true.

40:11.575 --> 40:12.451
Ta-da.

40:12.535 --> 40:14.995
Dried persimmons. Your favorite.

40:15.079 --> 40:16.330
Yeah, they're good.

40:17.790 --> 40:19.792
- They're from Sangju.
- Yeah.

40:21.752 --> 40:23.921
Dad, do you like it here?

40:24.547 --> 40:25.381
Tastes good.

40:27.174 --> 40:29.844
It's much nicer than before, right?

40:33.472 --> 40:34.306
Dad?

40:35.850 --> 40:37.017
I'm sorry.

40:37.977 --> 40:39.854
That will never happen again.

40:39.937 --> 40:40.938
Don't worry, okay?

41:01.625 --> 41:02.710
Dad, who did--

41:02.793 --> 41:04.128
"Don't worry, Father."

41:04.962 --> 41:09.175
"No matter what happens,
I'll protect you and Hee-joo."

41:18.726 --> 41:20.227
He came here?

41:35.242 --> 41:36.285
Warm, right?

41:39.872 --> 41:42.583
So warm, yet so cold.

41:43.751 --> 41:45.878
So harsh, yet so kind.

41:48.506 --> 41:50.299
I can't figure him out.

41:51.634 --> 41:54.136
I thought I knew him well,

41:55.304 --> 41:57.097
but I don't think I do at all.

42:05.523 --> 42:08.359
Today's sign language interpreter
interview evaluation.

42:09.151 --> 42:10.861
Is the press release ready?

42:10.945 --> 42:11.987
It's being finalized.

42:13.447 --> 42:14.323
By the way,

42:15.074 --> 42:18.327
about interpreter Hong Hee-joo
who had an interview earlier,

42:18.410 --> 42:22.331
were you pleased with her or not?

42:22.414 --> 42:24.208
Why do you want to know that?

42:24.291 --> 42:25.125
Excuse me?

42:26.001 --> 42:27.461
Because…

42:29.922 --> 42:35.010
Everyone found out
you turned the interview room upside down,

42:35.094 --> 42:37.346
so we made a bet for fun…

42:37.429 --> 42:38.556
A bet?

42:38.639 --> 42:39.807
For fun?

42:39.890 --> 42:42.893
We were about to, but we decided not to,
and we won't.

42:42.977 --> 42:45.145
What? A bet? No way.

42:45.229 --> 42:48.023
In this crucial decision
to select an interpreter

42:48.107 --> 42:50.025
to be the voice of our office…

42:56.532 --> 42:57.992
By the way, I like her.

42:59.910 --> 43:03.372
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo,
who studied you so passionately.

43:10.004 --> 43:10.838
So do I.

43:13.465 --> 43:14.341
I like her.

43:15.342 --> 43:16.468
Pardon?

43:32.359 --> 43:34.111
HONG HEE-JOO

43:41.160 --> 43:42.036
Congratulations.

43:42.119 --> 43:43.495
Thank you.

44:22.159 --> 44:23.452
You didn't eat anything.

44:23.535 --> 44:27.289
Not eating as an invited guest
is considered disrespectful.

44:28.874 --> 44:29.750
Eat it.

44:32.419 --> 44:33.545
My son…

44:35.422 --> 44:36.799
likes fish.

45:01.448 --> 45:02.574
Stop stuffing your face!

45:03.700 --> 45:05.911
I didn't eat anything yet.

45:07.371 --> 45:09.206
I told you not to act pathetic.

45:12.167 --> 45:14.044
Learn from your sister.

45:31.603 --> 45:32.438
Let's switch.

45:36.024 --> 45:36.900
Eat it.

45:52.875 --> 45:54.042
Slow down.

45:58.005 --> 45:59.089
What's your name?

46:05.053 --> 46:05.888
"Hong."

46:07.014 --> 46:07.848
"Hee."

46:09.975 --> 46:10.809
"Joo."

46:10.893 --> 46:11.727
HONG HEE-JOO

46:12.561 --> 46:13.395
"Hong Hee-joo"?

46:24.072 --> 46:25.657
When did you grow up so much?

46:35.542 --> 46:36.793
Thank you.

46:37.794 --> 46:39.963
You changed my dad's nursing home.

46:44.885 --> 46:46.386
He read it right away.

46:58.565 --> 47:00.901
HONG IN-A

47:18.794 --> 47:20.128
What are you saying?

47:20.212 --> 47:23.340
You want me to go in In-a's place
at the wedding tomorrow?

47:23.423 --> 47:25.425
Have you ever imagined that, Hee-joo?

47:25.509 --> 47:27.678
You and I come from humble beginnings,

47:27.761 --> 47:31.306
and now we'll be
the future president's in-laws!

48:02.754 --> 48:03.630
Keep it safe.

48:08.552 --> 48:09.886
If the real owner returns,

48:10.596 --> 48:12.180
you might have to give it back.

48:45.380 --> 48:46.381
Start.

48:48.884 --> 48:50.010
SA-EON

48:51.178 --> 48:53.764
What? Right now? At this hour?

48:54.348 --> 48:55.182
Why?

48:55.724 --> 48:59.061
No, wait. Don't overthink it.
Just answer it.

49:04.066 --> 49:06.068
Hello? Sa-eon?

49:06.151 --> 49:08.320
Hey, it's me. I only have three minutes.

49:08.403 --> 49:09.363
I'll make it quick.

49:09.446 --> 49:10.405
Oh, my.

49:11.239 --> 49:14.242
By chance, did you just add water
to your cup noodles too?

49:14.326 --> 49:16.119
No, I'm driving.

49:16.203 --> 49:18.288
Oh, I see.

49:18.372 --> 49:19.998
Ji Sang-woo I met the other day.

49:20.082 --> 49:21.958
- He's doing a program with you, right?
- Yes.

49:23.168 --> 49:26.380
Age 34. Yeonhui University College
of Medicine, class of 2010.

49:26.463 --> 49:29.132
Director of Bliss Care Clinic.
Do you know anything else about him?

49:30.759 --> 49:33.053
Did you run a background check on him?

49:33.136 --> 49:36.056
Do you know anything about him
that's not on the website?

49:36.139 --> 49:37.516
I have two minutes left.

49:39.351 --> 49:41.353
Well…

49:42.062 --> 49:44.064
Right. He lives in Yeouido.

49:44.147 --> 49:45.190
Near the HBC building.

49:45.899 --> 49:47.234
- And.
- And?

49:47.859 --> 49:49.569
And…

49:49.653 --> 49:51.154
He grew up in an orphanage!

49:51.863 --> 49:52.823
An orphanage?

49:52.906 --> 49:55.075
No! Never mind!

49:57.828 --> 49:59.121
NURI DREAM CENTER

50:00.455 --> 50:02.332
Is it Nuri Dream Center?

50:03.083 --> 50:05.168
Formerly known as Sinil Childcare Center?

50:05.752 --> 50:06.837
How did you know?

50:09.548 --> 50:10.424
But…

50:11.007 --> 50:12.634
why do you want to know?

50:12.718 --> 50:13.677
I'm out of time.

50:13.760 --> 50:15.053
Enjoy your noodles.

50:26.189 --> 50:27.983
It seems you messed up again, 406.

50:28.567 --> 50:29.735
You asked me before,

50:30.402 --> 50:34.197
what do I get in return
if you get rid of Hong Hee-joo?

50:34.865 --> 50:37.284
I'll answer that question.

50:38.827 --> 50:39.745
What is it?

50:41.371 --> 50:42.205
Hong In-a.

50:50.297 --> 50:52.507
In-a needs a place to return to.

50:53.300 --> 50:56.011
You and your family wanted

50:56.094 --> 50:58.472
Hong In-a from the start anyway.

50:58.555 --> 50:59.806
Hong Hee-joo…

51:02.184 --> 51:04.519
is just a stand-in puppet.

51:07.189 --> 51:08.023
There.

51:09.232 --> 51:11.276
So get rid of Hong Hee-joo.

51:12.027 --> 51:14.654
Before Hong In-a returns
and complicates things,

51:14.738 --> 51:18.658
- take care of Hong Hee-joo--
- 406, you don't know anything.

51:18.742 --> 51:19.993
What?

51:22.287 --> 51:24.498
I'll only say this once,
so listen carefully.

51:25.499 --> 51:26.958
Before Hong In-a disappeared,

51:27.042 --> 51:29.669
the last person she met with
before the wedding

51:29.753 --> 51:30.754
was me.

51:33.590 --> 51:34.466
What?

51:36.134 --> 51:38.845
I guess you didn't dig that deep.

51:40.722 --> 51:41.556
When you two met,

51:42.682 --> 51:44.100
what did you talk about?

51:44.184 --> 51:45.310
We made a deal.

51:46.978 --> 51:48.021
What deal?

51:48.647 --> 51:50.065
Because of that deal,

51:50.148 --> 51:54.069
Hong In-a can never become
Paik Sa-eon's wife.

51:54.986 --> 51:56.112
What now?

51:56.822 --> 51:59.407
I think I just got rid of
your motive for blackmail.

52:05.330 --> 52:06.706
He met with In-a?

52:07.290 --> 52:10.126
They made a deal? What deal?

52:26.935 --> 52:28.103
You're still up?

52:29.145 --> 52:32.566
I thought you'd be sleeping
after the stressful day you had today.

52:35.944 --> 52:38.613
I owe you an apology
for underestimating you.

52:39.906 --> 52:41.199
You did great.

52:44.160 --> 52:46.788
But the official results
haven't been announced yet.

52:46.872 --> 52:48.498
So don't get ahead of yourself.

52:51.001 --> 52:51.835
Also,

52:52.335 --> 52:55.463
I'm attending the Chungwoon Daily News
anniversary event tomorrow.

53:01.511 --> 53:02.679
Why all of a sudden?

53:03.680 --> 53:05.515
Do you know or not

53:06.474 --> 53:08.143
that my sister is back?

53:08.727 --> 53:10.312
You look beautiful.

53:13.148 --> 53:15.483
- Hello.
- Hi, so pretty.

53:15.567 --> 53:17.569
You know what day it is today, right?

53:17.652 --> 53:19.279
I want something special.

53:19.362 --> 53:20.739
Hello.

53:23.158 --> 53:24.326
Look who it is.

53:24.826 --> 53:25.994
Hello.

53:26.870 --> 53:27.913
Ms. Lee.

53:27.996 --> 53:30.332
Can you have two clients
in one room like this?

53:31.082 --> 53:33.084
I'm sorry. Show her to the waiting room.

53:37.631 --> 53:39.341
We're a family.

53:40.842 --> 53:44.804
You're always so busy.
I didn't think you'd make it to the event.

53:44.888 --> 53:47.057
Just like last time,

53:47.140 --> 53:50.226
I thought your husband
would be coming with a cute aide.

54:08.161 --> 54:09.955
I want my hair to be higher than hers.

54:10.038 --> 54:11.748
Make my eyeliner wings longer too!

54:14.125 --> 54:16.670
CHUNGWOON DAILY NEWS
LEADING THE ERA, UNITING GENERATIONS

54:16.753 --> 54:18.630
CHUNGWOON CULTURAL FOUNDATION SCHOLARSHIP

54:21.341 --> 54:23.301
CHUNGWOON
LEADING THE ERA, UNITING GENERATIONS

54:33.687 --> 54:36.106
CHUNGWOON DAILY NEWS
70TH ANNIVERSARY CELEBRATION

54:36.189 --> 54:38.149
WITH THE PEOPLE
CHUNGWOON DAILY NEWS

54:39.484 --> 54:41.069
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

54:44.114 --> 54:46.866
We'll begin the cutting of the cake.

55:13.101 --> 55:14.269
Congratulations.

55:14.936 --> 55:17.814
I wish you infinite success
and development in the future.

55:17.897 --> 55:19.691
Thank you so much.

55:19.774 --> 55:22.569
You're the busiest man in our country,
yet you made it.

55:22.652 --> 55:24.029
You flatter me.

55:24.112 --> 55:26.823
We wouldn't miss
such a meaningful and joyous day.

55:29.117 --> 55:29.951
But…

55:30.535 --> 55:32.370
I don't see our spokesperson yet.

55:35.081 --> 55:38.710
I wonder if the presidential office
is looking for a successor.

55:38.793 --> 55:41.212
If he wants to join
the presidential campaign,

55:41.963 --> 55:44.007
isn't it time he left his position?

55:44.090 --> 55:45.341
Of course.

55:46.217 --> 55:49.596
But as you know, he has so much ambition.

55:50.346 --> 55:53.058
I'm not sure if he'll give up his career
and join me.

55:53.725 --> 55:57.062
But still,
I'll try harder to convince him.

56:00.690 --> 56:02.734
How delightful.

56:04.277 --> 56:05.111
Yes, okay.

56:28.927 --> 56:29.844
Hee-joo.

56:36.059 --> 56:37.977
Come with me.

56:59.499 --> 57:02.877
What's this about your dad?
The hospital called and said he was moved.

57:02.961 --> 57:03.795
Is that true?

57:09.050 --> 57:10.760
Your son-in-law moved him.

57:12.095 --> 57:13.304
He did?

57:13.388 --> 57:16.850
Are you telling me
he found out about your dad?

57:19.853 --> 57:21.479
How could you let that happen?

57:21.563 --> 57:23.148
What if the chairman finds out?

57:26.860 --> 57:30.363
Aren't you going to ask why he was moved
or what happened to him?

57:31.948 --> 57:32.824
I don't care.

57:32.907 --> 57:36.494
Anyway, now that he's been moved,
I don't need to pay anymore, right?

57:44.043 --> 57:45.044
That's much better.

57:49.340 --> 57:50.550
Did you see Sa-eon?

57:51.259 --> 57:53.136
He's in a whole different class now.

57:53.219 --> 57:54.929
I know, right?

57:55.013 --> 57:56.598
Is In-a not coming again today?

57:56.681 --> 57:59.642
She hasn't shown her face in public
since she got married.

58:00.310 --> 58:03.313
The president's daughter-in-law,
someone of great importance.

58:03.396 --> 58:04.314
Such a big deal.

58:05.231 --> 58:06.941
But In-a's sister is here.

58:07.025 --> 58:10.820
- She's such an attention-seeker.
- I always found her a bit off.

58:10.904 --> 58:13.823
She followed In-a around like a shadow.
So creepy.

58:14.532 --> 58:17.160
- Another glass of wine?
- Shall we? Let's go.

58:58.243 --> 58:59.077
Must be nice.

58:59.160 --> 59:00.995
- Let's toast.
- Cheers.

01:00:06.561 --> 01:00:09.188
CALLS
PAIK SA-EON

01:00:22.118 --> 01:00:22.952
PAIK SA-EON

01:00:58.571 --> 01:01:00.740
406, Hong Hee-joo.

01:01:02.909 --> 01:01:05.244
He must not care about either.

01:01:11.834 --> 01:01:12.752
Hello?

01:01:17.215 --> 01:01:18.216
Speak.

01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:28.810
Your fiancée disappeared

01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:31.979
the day before the wedding,

01:01:33.856 --> 01:01:36.067
and Hong Hee-joo stepped in instead.

01:01:39.696 --> 01:01:40.905
How did you feel?

01:01:44.867 --> 01:01:46.494
Well, I get it.

01:01:46.577 --> 01:01:48.287
I'm sure it wasn't great.

01:01:51.666 --> 01:01:52.625
It was similar.

01:01:58.464 --> 01:01:59.298
Right.

01:02:00.550 --> 01:02:03.219
What use is she? Who else would take her?

01:02:04.011 --> 01:02:05.430
She's gloomy.

01:02:06.639 --> 01:02:08.808
She has no social skills.

01:02:10.518 --> 01:02:11.769
She's just…

01:02:15.189 --> 01:02:17.900
the supplementary pages
that came with Hong In-a.

01:02:19.277 --> 01:02:20.111
Yeah.

01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:22.488
That's what she is.

01:02:24.282 --> 01:02:25.783
Do you know what's funnier?

01:02:26.451 --> 01:02:28.327
She always knew that too.

01:02:30.163 --> 01:02:33.666
But she hesitated each time
even though she wanted to break free.

01:02:37.170 --> 01:02:39.213
She didn't have the courage.

01:02:39.297 --> 01:02:42.175
She hated rich families
but was comforted by luxury.

01:02:43.009 --> 01:02:45.470
She cowardly succumbed to money.

01:02:57.523 --> 01:02:58.441
Hello?

01:03:03.154 --> 01:03:04.071
Hee-joo…

01:03:06.199 --> 01:03:07.533
isn't gloomy.

01:03:08.785 --> 01:03:10.787
She's observing her surroundings.

01:03:11.871 --> 01:03:13.456
She doesn't lack social skills.

01:03:14.749 --> 01:03:16.834
In general, people are rude to her first.

01:03:18.169 --> 01:03:19.921
Also, she didn't succumb to money.

01:03:23.007 --> 01:03:23.925
She just…

01:03:25.426 --> 01:03:26.969
loved her mother.

01:03:30.848 --> 01:03:31.849
There was a time

01:03:32.558 --> 01:03:36.312
when I hated to eat or speak
with my mouth.

01:03:37.688 --> 01:03:43.069
I was surrounded by greedy,
noisy, and bothersome people.

01:03:44.779 --> 01:03:46.280
And she was the most quiet.

01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:50.326
When I stared at her…

01:03:52.495 --> 01:03:54.580
strangely, I could breathe easily.

01:03:59.293 --> 01:04:00.294
What did you say?

01:04:01.003 --> 01:04:02.171
Supplementary pages?

01:04:03.756 --> 01:04:05.424
If you don't know, listen carefully, 406.

01:04:06.050 --> 01:04:07.885
Hee-joo isn't supplementary pages.

01:04:07.969 --> 01:04:09.762
She's a brand-new language.

01:04:10.429 --> 01:04:14.433
She's repeated the same hand movements
thousands of times to become who she is.

01:04:15.309 --> 01:04:16.769
People don't know that.

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:20.439
So don't talk about my wife like that.

01:04:22.275 --> 01:04:25.278
Then why did you treat her
like she was invisible?

01:04:27.530 --> 01:04:30.825
You say you know her so well,
then why did you do that?

01:04:32.159 --> 01:04:34.954
Why did you tell her
not to think you were a couple?

01:05:16.537 --> 01:05:19.457
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:05:19.540 --> 01:05:21.208
Okay, I'll take it now.

01:05:21.292 --> 01:05:23.044
One, two, three!

01:05:24.086 --> 01:05:25.630
That was nice. One more.

01:05:25.713 --> 01:05:28.049
Wait. Can I shake your hand?

01:05:28.716 --> 01:05:29.550
Of course.

01:05:32.053 --> 01:05:34.055
Okay. One, two, three!

01:05:36.390 --> 01:05:38.017
Thank you so much.

01:05:39.185 --> 01:05:40.561
It came out great.

01:05:41.312 --> 01:05:43.397
My wife will love this.

01:05:43.481 --> 01:05:44.482
Sure.

01:05:45.816 --> 01:05:48.361
Then, the report…

01:05:48.444 --> 01:05:49.320
That's right.

01:05:53.699 --> 01:05:54.825
I almost forgot.

01:05:54.909 --> 01:05:57.328
Is your wife okay?

01:05:58.579 --> 01:05:59.413
Thanks to you.

01:05:59.497 --> 01:06:01.749
Thank you for your concern.

01:06:01.832 --> 01:06:03.292
We're relieved to hear it.

01:06:03.376 --> 01:06:06.253
She was so shocked that day.

01:06:06.337 --> 01:06:08.839
I thought she was having a panic attack.

01:06:10.216 --> 01:06:11.801
A panic attack?

01:06:11.884 --> 01:06:12.927
Yes.

01:06:13.010 --> 01:06:16.097
She was like…

01:06:16.180 --> 01:06:17.264
Her face got so pale.

01:06:17.348 --> 01:06:20.309
She was screaming so loudly too.

01:06:20.393 --> 01:06:22.311
We were on the road then,

01:06:22.395 --> 01:06:24.230
but I pulled over and let her out.

01:06:24.313 --> 01:06:26.649
It would've been bad if we hadn't.

01:06:27.566 --> 01:06:28.401
Wait.

01:06:30.111 --> 01:06:31.904
What did you just say?

01:06:33.280 --> 01:06:34.115
What?

01:06:36.033 --> 01:06:36.993
Well…

01:06:39.328 --> 01:06:41.580
- A panic…
- No, not that.

01:06:44.333 --> 01:06:46.335
She screamed?

01:06:48.129 --> 01:06:49.088
My wife did?

01:06:58.264 --> 01:06:59.223
What is it?

01:06:59.306 --> 01:07:00.141
What's wrong?

01:07:00.850 --> 01:07:03.185
- What…
- Are you feeling sick?

01:07:05.646 --> 01:07:06.981
Let me out.

01:07:09.775 --> 01:07:10.860
Let me out.

01:07:11.777 --> 01:07:13.696
We're on the road right now.

01:07:13.779 --> 01:07:15.698
It'll be okay if you just let me out.

01:07:15.781 --> 01:07:17.575
It'll be okay, so let me out!

01:07:17.658 --> 01:07:19.493
Please, let me out!

01:07:41.807 --> 01:07:44.101
I can't do this. Just let me out.

01:07:46.520 --> 01:07:48.856
Just let me out.

01:07:54.820 --> 01:07:56.614
Please, let me out!

01:08:56.632 --> 01:08:59.552
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:09:01.387 --> 01:09:02.555
Why did you go that far?

01:09:03.305 --> 01:09:06.058
Don't you have any?
Something you're hiding from me.

01:09:07.518 --> 01:09:10.271
This is great for Hee-joo!
She's going to the presidential office.

01:09:10.354 --> 01:09:14.316
What's a good gift
to give someone who just got a job?

01:09:15.860 --> 01:09:18.320
I look forward to working with you.

01:09:19.280 --> 01:09:20.114
Don't be surprised.

01:09:20.614 --> 01:09:21.991
Gender of 406 is…

01:09:22.074 --> 01:09:23.492
- A woman?
- Paik Sa-eon!

01:09:32.376 --> 01:09:34.378
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
